"""Render complete refusal-scan deltas; Part 1 is appended after its census."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
OUT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
p=json.loads((OUT/'pairing.json').read_text());new=json.loads((OUT/'new-findings-attributed.json').read_text())
lines=['# c4v-7 census','','sys.ts:304:13: Part 1 pending. scanner.ts:2934:41: Part 1 pending. **'+str(p['new'])+' new refusal-scan findings.**','','Head: `1d48ecb5a5321717daf901579e49a23291995589`; main and confirmed merge-base: `5c8338c4232c37afb304ce6865458b67655c590a`. Measurement and reporting only; no adaptation or compiler changes.','','## Part 2 — paired refusal scan','','All 79 adapted compiler files at each commit, CommonJSBundle. Scan-only sees refusal-scan findings only; all 4,397 main and 4,024 head findings have phase `refusal_scan`. It does not lower bodies. The full first-stop census is needed to name lowering-phase stops. All controls and per-file output validations passed.','','The adapted source identity check is in [source-identity.json](source-identity.json). Finding identity is `(kind, file, line, column, reason)`. Paths are normalized to `src/compiler/`; identical lines map by identity. “Changed” means the same key has different normalized diagnostic text; reason/kind changes count as gone plus new.','','| Before | After | Gone | New | Changed |','| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |',f"| {p['before']} | {p['after']} | {p['gone']} | {p['new']} | {p['changed']} |",'','| Reason | Gone | New | Changed |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for reason,c in p['by_reason'].items():
 if c['gone'] or c['new'] or c['changed']:lines.append('| '+reason.replace('|','\\|')+f" | {c['gone']} | {c['new']} | {c['changed']} |")
s=p['selected_191'];lines+=['',f"Of the scout’s 191 selected ‘seen as’ sites, {s['present_before']} are present on main, **{s['gone']} are gone on head** ({s['removed_by_head']} removed by this head versus main), and {s['present_after']} remain on head. The older scout’s sys.ts:307:13 maps to main/head sys.ts:304:13, proven by reconstructing the scout’s full sys.ts source hash from its owner pins; the other 190 sites use byte-identical source files. See [scout-site-mapping.json](scout-site-mapping.json). Exact key membership is preserved in [selected-191-pairing.json](selected-191-pairing.json).",'','Full counts by reason, including zero-delta reasons, are in [pairing.json](pairing.json). Complete raw streams and process statuses are under `part2/`; all gone/new/changed diagnostics are retained as JSON.','','## Every new finding','',f"New findings inside a generic body: {sum(bool(f['generic_bodies']) for f in new)}. Full enclosing function chains and bound call slots are recorded below.",'']
for i,f in enumerate(new,1):
 owner=f['enclosing_function'];generics=f['generic_bodies']
 rule=f.get('registered_rule')
 lines += [f"### {i}. {f['where']}",'',f"Kind: `{f['kind']}`. Rule: `{f['rule'] or 'none emitted'}`. Phase: `{f['phase']}`.",'','Reason: '+f['reason'],'','Text:','','```text',f['raw_text'],'```','','Adapted source line:','','```typescript',f['source_line'],'```','','Enclosing function: '+(f"`{owner['name']}` at `{owner['where']}`" if owner else 'module scope')+'.']
 if f.get('enclosing_functions'):lines+=['','Enclosing function chain: '+ ' → '.join('`'+g['name']+'` (`'+g['where']+'`)' for g in f['enclosing_functions'])+'.']
 if f.get('diagnostic_emitter'):lines+=['','Diagnostic emitter: `'+f['diagnostic_emitter']['name']+'` at `'+f['diagnostic_emitter']['source']+'`.']
 if rule:lines+=['','Registered rule: `'+str(rule['order'])+' '+rule['name']+'`; emitter `'+rule['emitter']+'` at `'+rule['emitter_source']+'`.']
 if f.get('binding'):lines+=['','Binding judged at the call: `'+json.dumps(f['binding'],ensure_ascii=False)+'`.']
 if generics:
  for g in generics:lines+=['','Generic body: `'+g['name']+'` at `'+g['where']+'`; parameters: `'+', '.join(g['typeParameters'])+'`.']
  lines+=['','Slot at the finding: `'+json.dumps(f['slot'],ensure_ascii=False)+'`.']
 else:lines+=['','The finding is outside a generic body.']
 if not generics and f.get('slot'):lines+=['','Syntactic slot context: `'+json.dumps(f['slot'],ensure_ascii=False)+'`.']
 lines+=['']
lines+=['## Setup and bounds','','Fresh detached worktrees per measured commit were created in writable scratch. Recursive submodules initialized successfully at both commits; no credential error occurred. Upstream TypeScript HEAD and peeled v6.0.3 both equal `050880ce59e30b356b686bd3144efe24f875ebc8`. Each stage3/api install passed. The initial npm calls used the default npm cache; they were repeated successfully with an explicit scratch cache and logs. All census inputs, overlays, outputs, build products, Go caches, and subsequent npm caches use scratch. The shared checkout was not modified.','','The scan wrapper was copied from `typescript/promise-discard-sites` at `2dc0593b937f8fbaf6c32f8107a899f78c223966`. That branch has no promise-discard-sites README; its REPORT.md and the latent README document the procedure. Each scan binary was built once. All 158 actual compiler-file headers have `checker_rejected: false` and zero diagnostics. The fixed legacy measurement label “measured on a checker-rejected program” does not describe the input status. The inherited raw header says `latent_mode: first-error`; this label was not rewritten, while the scratch driver explicitly calls `LatentScanOnly` and zero lowering units are checked. Scratch overlays alone replace the driver call with `LatentScanOnly`; ordinary Lower remains disabled and output guards are enabled. Each compiler-file process has a 1,500-second process-group bound and cleanup; at most three run concurrently. A non-forced checkpoint push follows every batch of at most ten paired files.','','## Part 1','','Pending; Part 2 was completed and pushed first. The 5c8338c4 evidence branch contains the CommonJSBundle baseline, but says EcmaScript has not started. No EcmaScript baseline will be invented.']
(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
